diff --git a/features/add-and-display-todos.feature b/features/add-and-display-todos.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..1f7c9f5
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/add-and-display-todos.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,43 @@
+Feature: Add and display todos
+  As a user
+  I want to add todos and see them listed
+  So that I can track what needs to be done
+
+  Background:
+    Given the TodoMVC app is open
+
+  Scenario: Page loads with focused input and hidden main and footer
+    Then the new-todo input is focused
+    And the main section is hidden
+    And the footer section is hidden
+
+  Scenario: Create a todo by pressing Enter
+    When the user types "Buy groceries" in the new-todo input and presses Enter
+    Then the todo list contains 1 item
+    And the todo at position 1 has title "Buy groceries"
+    And the todo at position 1 is not completed
+    And the new-todo input is empty
+    And the main section is visible
+    And the footer section is visible
+
+  Scenario: Create multiple todos
+    When the user types "Buy groceries" in the new-todo input and presses Enter
+    And the user types "Walk the dog" in the new-todo input and presses Enter
+    Then the todo list contains 2 items
+    And the todo at position 1 has title "Buy groceries"
+    And the todo at position 2 has title "Walk the dog"
+
+  Scenario: Empty or whitespace input is ignored
+    When the user types "" in the new-todo input and presses Enter
+    Then the todo list contains 0 items
+    When the user types "   " in the new-todo input and presses Enter
+    Then the todo list contains 0 items
+
+  Scenario: Input is trimmed before creating todo
+    When the user types "  Buy groceries  " in the new-todo input and presses Enter
+    Then the todo at position 1 has title "Buy groceries"
+
+  Scenario: Footer shows correct count after adding todos
+    When the user types "Buy groceries" in the new-todo input and presses Enter
+    And the user types "Walk the dog" in the new-todo input and presses Enter
+    Then the active count displays "2 items left"
diff --git a/features/edit-todo.feature b/features/edit-todo.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..a3c2535
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/edit-todo.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,47 @@
+Feature: Edit a todo
+  As a user
+  I want to double-click a todo to edit its title
+  So that I can correct or update my tasks
+
+  Background:
+    Given the TodoMVC app is open
+    And the user has created a todo "Buy groceries"
+
+  Scenario: Double-click activates editing mode
+    When the user double-clicks the todo at position 1
+    Then the todo at position 1 has the editing class
+    And the edit input at position 1 contains "Buy groceries"
+    And the edit input at position 1 is focused
+
+  Scenario: Save edit on Enter
+    When the user double-clicks the todo at position 1
+    And the user types "Buy organic groceries" in the edit input at position 1 and presses Enter
+    Then the todo at position 1 has title "Buy organic groceries"
+    And the todo at position 1 does not have the editing class
+
+  Scenario: Save edit on blur
+    When the user double-clicks the todo at position 1
+    And the user types "Buy organic groceries" in the edit input at position 1 and blurs
+    Then the todo at position 1 has title "Buy organic groceries"
+    And the todo at position 1 does not have the editing class
+
+  Scenario: Escape discards changes
+    When the user double-clicks the todo at position 1
+    And the user types "Buy organic groceries" in the edit input at position 1 and presses Escape
+    Then the todo at position 1 has title "Buy groceries"
+    And the todo at position 1 does not have the editing class
+
+  Scenario: Empty edit destroys the todo
+    When the user double-clicks the todo at position 1
+    And the user clears the edit input at position 1 and presses Enter
+    Then the todo list contains 0 items
+
+  Scenario: Whitespace-only edit destroys the todo
+    When the user double-clicks the todo at position 1
+    And the user types "   " in the edit input at position 1 and presses Enter
+    Then the todo list contains 0 items
+
+  Scenario: Edit is trimmed before saving
+    When the user double-clicks the todo at position 1
+    And the user types "  Organic groceries  " in the edit input at position 1 and presses Enter
+    Then the todo at position 1 has title "Organic groceries"
diff --git a/features/footer.feature b/features/footer.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..68a021b
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/footer.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,52 @@
+Feature: Footer controls
+  As a user
+  I want a footer with count, filters, and clear-completed
+  So that I can manage my todo list at a glance
+
+  Background:
+    Given the TodoMVC app is open
+
+  Scenario: Active count shows singular for one item
+    When the user types "Buy groceries" in the new-todo input and presses Enter
+    Then the active count displays "1 item left"
+
+  Scenario: Active count shows plural for multiple items
+    When the user types "Buy groceries" in the new-todo input and presses Enter
+    And the user types "Walk the dog" in the new-todo input and presses Enter
+    Then the active count displays "2 items left"
+
+  Scenario: Active count reflects completed todos
+    When the user types "Buy groceries" in the new-todo input and presses Enter
+    And the user types "Walk the dog" in the new-todo input and presses Enter
+    And the user toggles the todo at position 1
+    Then the active count displays "1 item left"
+
+  Scenario: Clear completed button removes completed todos
+    When the user types "Buy groceries" in the new-todo input and presses Enter
+    And the user types "Walk the dog" in the new-todo input and presses Enter
+    And the user toggles the todo at position 1
+    And the user clicks the "Clear completed" button
+    Then the todo list contains 1 item
+    And the todo at position 1 has title "Walk the dog"
+
+  Scenario: Clear completed is hidden when no todos are completed
+    Then the "Clear completed" button is hidden
+
+  Scenario: Clear completed is visible when some todos are completed
+    When the user types "Buy groceries" in the new-todo input and presses Enter
+    And the user toggles the todo at position 1
+    Then the "Clear completed" button is visible
+
+  Scenario: Clear completed does not affect active todos
+    When the user types "Buy groceries" in the new-todo input and presses Enter
+    And the user types "Walk the dog" in the new-todo input and presses Enter
+    And the user toggles the todo at position 1
+    And the user clicks the "Clear completed" button
+    Then the active count displays "1 item left"
+
+  Scenario: Footer hidden when no todos exist
+    Then the footer section is hidden
+
+  Scenario: Footer visible when todos exist
+    When the user types "Buy groceries" in the new-todo input and presses Enter
+    Then the footer section is visible
diff --git a/features/persistence.feature b/features/persistence.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..319c294
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/persistence.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,27 @@
+Feature: localStorage persistence
+  As a user
+  I want my todos to persist across page reloads
+  So that I do not lose my work
+
+  Background:
+    Given the TodoMVC app is open
+
+  Scenario: Todos survive page reload
+    When the user types "Buy groceries" in the new-todo input and presses Enter
+    And the user types "Walk the dog" in the new-todo input and presses Enter
+    And the page reloads
+    Then the todo list contains 2 items
+    And the todo at position 1 has title "Buy groceries"
+    And the todo at position 2 has title "Walk the dog"
+
+  Scenario: Completion state survives page reload
+    When the user types "Buy groceries" in the new-todo input and presses Enter
+    And the user toggles the todo at position 1
+    And the page reloads
+    Then the todo at position 1 is completed
+
+  Scenario: Filter survives page reload
+    When the user types "Buy groceries" in the new-todo input and presses Enter
+    And the user navigates to "#/active"
+    And the page reloads
+    Then the "Active" filter link is selected
diff --git a/features/routing.feature b/features/routing.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..8073a8f
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/routing.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,42 @@
+Feature: Routing and filtering
+  As a user
+  I want to filter my todos by status
+  So that I can focus on active or completed work
+
+  Background:
+    Given the TodoMVC app is open
+    And the user has created todos "Buy groceries" and "Walk the dog"
+    And the user has toggled the todo at position 1
+
+  Scenario: All filter shows all todos
+    When the user navigates to "#/"
+    Then the todo list displays 2 items
+    And the "All" filter link is selected
+
+  Scenario: Active filter shows only active todos
+    When the user navigates to "#/active"
+    Then the todo list displays 1 item
+    And the visible todo has title "Walk the dog"
+    And the "Active" filter link is selected
+
+  Scenario: Completed filter shows only completed todos
+    When the user navigates to "#/completed"
+    Then the todo list displays 1 item
+    And the visible todo has title "Buy groceries"
+    And the "Completed" filter link is selected
+
+  Scenario: Default route shows all todos
+    When the user navigates to ""
+    Then the todo list displays 2 items
+    And the "All" filter link is selected
+
+  Scenario: Toggling a todo in filtered view hides it when filter does not match
+    Given the user navigates to "#/active"
+    When the user toggles the todo at position 1
+    Then the todo list displays 0 items
+
+  Scenario: Active filter is persisted on reload
+    When the user navigates to "#/active"
+    And the page reloads
+    Then the "Active" filter link is selected
+    And the todo list displays 1 item
diff --git a/features/toggle-todo.feature b/features/toggle-todo.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..2b456ab
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/toggle-todo.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,42 @@
+Feature: Toggle todo completion
+  As a user
+  I want to mark todos as complete or active
+  So that I can track my progress
+
+  Background:
+    Given the TodoMVC app is open
+    And the user has created todos "Buy groceries" and "Walk the dog"
+
+  Scenario: Mark a todo as completed
+    When the user toggles the todo at position 1
+    Then the todo at position 1 is completed
+    And the todo at position 2 is not completed
+
+  Scenario: Mark a completed todo as active
+    When the user toggles the todo at position 1
+    And the user toggles the todo at position 1
+    Then the todo at position 1 is not completed
+
+  Scenario: Toggle all marks all todos as completed
+    When the user toggles the toggle-all checkbox
+    Then the todo at position 1 is completed
+    And the todo at position 2 is completed
+    And the toggle-all checkbox is checked
+
+  Scenario: Toggle all marks all todos as active
+    When the user toggles the todo at position 1
+    And the user toggles the toggle-all checkbox
+    Then the todo at position 1 is not completed
+    And the todo at position 2 is not completed
+    And the toggle-all checkbox is not checked
+
+  Scenario: Toggle-all reflects state when all individual todos are completed
+    When the user toggles the todo at position 1
+    And the user toggles the todo at position 2
+    Then the toggle-all checkbox is checked
+
+  Scenario: Active count updates when todos are toggled
+    When the user toggles the todo at position 1
+    Then the active count displays "1 item left"
+    When the user toggles the toggle-all checkbox
+    Then the active count displays "2 items left"
